-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/portugal_get_back_ep-200x198.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Get Back EP artwork - Portugal\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/portugal_get_back_ep-200x198.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/portugal_get_back_ep-580x575.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/portugal_get_back_ep-960x952.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/portugal_get_back_ep-768x762.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/portugal_get_back_ep-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/portugal_get_back_ep.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"9980\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/portugal_get_back_ep/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/portugal_get_back_ep.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,992\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Get Back EP artwork – Portugal\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/portugal_get_back_ep-960x952.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon portrait\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/japan_get_back/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxOTgiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTk4IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"198\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_get_back-198x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Get Back single artwork - Japan\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_get_back-198x200.jpg 198w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_get_back-575x580.jpg 575w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_get_back-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_get_back.jpg 711w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 198px) 100vw, 198px\" data-attachment-id=\"9567\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/japan_get_back/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_get_back.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"711,717\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Get Back single artwork – Japan\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/japan_get_back.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/israel_get_back/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTk4IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDE5OCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"198\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/israel_get_back-200x198.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Get Back single artwork - Israel\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/israel_get_back-200x198.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/israel_get_back-580x573.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/israel_get_back-960x948.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/israel_get_back-768x759.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/israel_get_back-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/israel_get_back.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"9489\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/israel_get_back/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/israel_get_back.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,988\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Get Back single artwork – Israel\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/israel_get_back-960x948.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/italy_get_back/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/italy_get_back-200x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Get Back single artwork - Italy\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/italy_get_back-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/italy_get_back-580x580.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/italy_get_back-66x66.jpg 66w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/italy_get_back.jpg 717w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"9511\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/italy_get_back/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/italy_get_back.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"717,717\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Get Back single artwork – Italy\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/italy_get_back.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/germany_get_back/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTkzIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDE5MyI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"193\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/germany_get_back-200x193.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Get Back single artwork - Germany\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/germany_get_back-200x193.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/germany_get_back-580x559.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/germany_get_back-960x925.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/germany_get_back-768x740.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/germany_get_back.jpg 1000w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"9422\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/releases/germany_get_back/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/germany_get_back.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,964\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Get Back single artwork – Germany\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/germany_get_back-960x925.jpg\"></a></div></figure></div><h2>In the studio</h2><p>The Beatles’ first studio recording of ‘Don’t Let Me Down’ was taped on <a href=\"/1969/01/21/get-back-let-it-be-sessions-day-12/\">21 January 1969</a> at Apple, although rehearsals of the song had been filmed earlier in the month at Twickenham Film Studios.</p><p>A version from <a href=\"/1969/01/22/get-back-let-it-be-sessions-day-13/\">the following day</a> was selected for inclusion in the unreleased <em>Get Back</em> album, along with a snippet of speech in which Lennon asked Starr to hit the cymbals hard after the intro, to “give me the courage to come screaming in.”</p><p>On <a href=\"/1969/01/28/get-back-let-it-be-sessions-day-19/\">28 January</a> The Beatles and Preston recorded the version which ended up on the <a href=\"/songs/get-back/\">‘Get Back’</a> single. They taped it twice again <a href=\"/1969/01/30/the-beatles-rooftop-concert-apple-building/\">two days later</a> on the roof of Apple, the first of which was included in the <em>Let It Be</em> film.</p><blockquote><div>We recorded it in the basement of Apple for <a href=\"/albums/let-it-be/\"><em>Let It Be</em></a> and later did it up on the roof for the film. We went through it quite a lot for this one. I sang harmony on it, which makes me wonder if I helped with a couple of words, but I don’t think so. It was John’s song.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Paul McCartney<br>\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/manyyearsfromnow\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Many Years From Now</em></a>, Barry Miles</div><p>An edit of the two rooftop performances was included on 2003’s <a href=\"/albums/let-it-be-naked/\"><em>Let It Be… Naked</em></a>, in place of <a href=\"/songs/dig-it/\">‘Dig It’</a> and <a href=\"/songs/maggie-mae/\">‘Maggie Mae’</a>.</p><div class=\"fab-forum-link\"><a href=\"/fab-forum/the-songs/dont-let-me-down/\">Discuss ‘Don’t Let Me Down’ on the Fab Forum »</a></div></div><div style=\"font-size: 12px; margin: 10px 0 10px 0;\"><strong>Published:</strong> <time itemprop=\"datePublished\" datetime=\"2008-03-14T17:19:50+00:00\" content=\"2008-03-14T17:19:50+00:00\">14 March 2008 </time> | <time itemprop=\"dateModified\" datetime=\"2026-07-30T13:50:34+01:00\" content=\"2026-07-30T13:50:34+01:00\"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 30 July 2026</time></div>",
  "textContent": "The Beatles’ songs – complete A-Z list » Don’t Let Me DownWritten by: Lennon-McCartney\nRecorded: 21, 22, 24, 27, 28, 29, 30 January 1969\nProducer: George Martin\nEngineer: Glyn JohnsReleased: 11 April 1969 (UK), 5 May 1969 (US)Available on:\nPast Masters\nLet It Be… NakedPersonnelJohn Lennon: vocals, rhythm guitar\nPaul McCartney: harmony vocals, bass\nGeorge Harrison: harmony vocals, lead guitar\nRingo Starr: drums\nBilly Preston: electric pianoAlthough just one new song – ‘Dig A Pony’ – by John Lennon made it onto the Let It Be album, he did compose ‘Don’t Let Me Down’, a love song to Yoko Ono, which was recorded during the same sessions and released as the b-side of the ‘Get Back’ single. As with Abbey Road’s ‘I Want You (She’s So Heavy)’, ‘Don’t Let Me Down’ was a lyrically simple and direct song inspired by his infatuation with Ono.When it gets down to it, when you’re drowning, you don’t say, “I would be incredibly pleased if someone would have the foresight to notice me drowning and come and help me,” you just scream.John Lennon\nRolling Stone, 1970Although Lennon was revealing his feelings and fears in song as far back as 1964’s ‘If I Fell’ and ‘I’m A Loser’, ‘Don’t Let Me Down’ was one of the first examples of the raw soul-baring that would reach a peak on ‘Cold Turkey’ and the John Lennon/Plastic Ono Band album.It was a very tense period: John was with Yoko and had escalated to heroin and all the accompanying paranoias and he was putting himself out on a limb. I think that as much as it excited and amused him, and the same time it secretly terrified him. So ‘Don’t Let Me Down’ was a genuine plea… It was saying to Yoko, ‘I’m really stepping out of line on this one. I’m really letting my vulnerability be seen, so you must not let me down.’ I think it was a genuine cry for help. It was a good song.Paul McCartney\nMany Years From Now, Barry Miles‘Don’t Let Me Down’ was released as the flip-side of ‘Get Back’ in the UK in April 1969, and in the US in May. Like its a-side, the song was credited to The Beatles with Billy Preston.Rod Stewart’s 1976 song ‘The Killing Of Georgie’ ends with a melody identical to ‘Don’t Let Me Down’, although Lennon later misidentified it as Stewart’s ‘Maggie May’.By the way, Rod Stewart turned ‘Don’t Let Me Down’ into [sings] ‘Maggie don’t go-o-o’ [sic]. That’s one that the publishers never noticed. Why didn’t he just sing ‘Don’t Let Me Down’? The same reason I don’t sing other people’s stuff, either: because you don’t get paid.John Lennon\nAll We Are Saying, David Sheff\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIn the studioThe Beatles’ first studio recording of ‘Don’t Let Me Down’ was taped on 21 January 1969 at Apple, although rehearsals of the song had been filmed earlier in the month at Twickenham Film Studios.A version from the following day was selected for inclusion in the unreleased Get Back album, along with a snippet of speech in which Lennon asked Starr to hit the cymbals hard after the intro, to “give me the courage to come screaming in.”On 28 January The Beatles and Preston recorded the version which ended up on the ‘Get Back’ single. They taped it twice again two days later on the roof of Apple, the first of which was included in the Let It Be film.We recorded it in the basement of Apple for Let It Be and later did it up on the roof for the film. We went through it quite a lot for this one. I sang harmony on it, which makes me wonder if I helped with a couple of words, but I don’t think so. It was John’s song.Paul McCartney\nMany Years From Now, Barry MilesAn edit of the two rooftop performances was included on 2003’s Let It Be… Naked, in place of ‘Dig It’ and ‘Maggie Mae’.Discuss ‘Don’t Let Me Down’ on the Fab Forum »Published: 14 March 2008  | Last updated: 30 July 2026",
